    a more fluent syntax.

    Besides the methods documented here you can combine queries using the
    binary AND and OR operators:

    >>> # Binary AND:
    >>> db.search((where('field1').exists()) & (where('field2') == 5))
    >>> # Binary OR:
    >>> db.search((where('field1').exists()) | (where('field2') == 5))

